cpplox
======

Prebuilt cpplox @PROJECT_VERSION@ interpreter. No installer is required - put
the binary anywhere on your PATH, or run it from this folder.

Quick start
-----------
  Windows:      cpplox.exe
  Linux/macOS:  ./cpplox

  cpplox myscript.lox    run a script
  cpplox                 start the REPL (type :q to exit)
  cpplox --version       print the version
  cpplox --help          print usage

Documentation
-------------
Language reference and examples for this version:
  https://github.com/IDragnev/cpplox/blob/v@PROJECT_VERSION@/README.md

Platform notes
--------------
  Windows x64: may require the Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributable
    https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/windows/latest-supported-vc-redist
    SmartScreen may warn on first run: More info -> Run anyway.

  Linux x64: needs a glibc and a libstdc++ at least as new as the ones it
    was built against; the release notes state which. Too old a system
    refuses to start it with a loader error naming the missing version,
    and building from source is the way round it.

  macOS arm64: requires macOS 11 (Big Sur) or newer, on Apple Silicon.
    The binary is unsigned, so the first launch needs Right-click -> Open,
    or clear the quarantine flag with: xattr -cr cpplox

